request: Make the output easier to read.

governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" doesn't describe a specific change I can test. The output comes from formatTodo/formatList in the format unit, and I can't see what it looks like now. Any change I picked would be a guess and might break the behaviour the existing tests pin down.)
governor asks: Which of these would make the output easier to read for you? Pick any, or describe your own:
1. Checkboxes instead of the current done marker, e.g. "[x] #3 Buy milk" and "[ ] #4 Call mom".
2. Lined-up columns: id, status, title and due date, with a header row.
3. Due dates in a readable form (e.g. "due Mon 3 Jun"), and "(overdue)" on past-due items.
4. Grouping: open todos first, then completed ones, with a blank line between them.
5. A summary line at the end, e.g. "2 open, 1 done".
6. A clear message when the list is empty, e.g. "No todos.".
7. Colour (ANSI), e.g. done items dimmed and overdue items in red. If so, should colour turn off when the output isn't a terminal?
Also, should the confirmation messages for add and complete change too, or only the list output?

